Doesn't sound like he's using the Mac OS X version of NetHack, but 
using OS X's 'classic' enironment to run the 3.4.1 binary for 
earlier versions of Mac OS. That version uses a file called 
"NetHack Defaults", in NetHack's directory, rather than a 
~/.nethackrc.

He may want to check (via "get info" in the finder) that the file 
hasn't had ".txt" (or .rtf) added to it by whatever editor he uses 
in Mac OS X, and remove the extension if it has.

